<!--
  NOT a download from a real Europass account, and nobody's CV. Written by hand for
  Postulo's tests on 2026-09-29 (#244), strictly from the European Commission's published
  schema for the Europass CV: "Europass XML schema definition v4.0.1"
  (https://europass.europa.eu/system/files/2020-07/ECV_DLV_20200714_4.0.1.zip, whose
  Candidate.xsd reads "Europass2 1.0.1, 02 June 2020") and the "EUROPASS2 CV XML Schema
  Documentation" v3.0.0
  (https://europass.europa.eu/system/files/2020-08/ECV_Schema_Documentation_v3.0.0_20200602.pdf),
  both fetched that day. It validates against that Candidate.xsd, and every element in it
  is one the schema defines, in the order it defines.

  It is the same invented person as europass.xml and europass.json, so that a test can
  insist the three formats read one career. Where this format says things differently it
  does so here too: a language is a code from the official list (as that list writes it,
  a Publications Office URI), a country is a code, and a job's description is HTML escaped
  inside the XML, which the documentation allows for its long texts.

  What europass.europa.eu actually puts in the PDF it hands out is described in #244, and
  is NOT this in every detail: real exports are reported to carry elements the schema does
  not define. The one real verification is a download, which is a person's to make.
-->
